# The first merge in the pre-sweep range that the x86 attribution named: 705 packs the request structures and pins the shared-memory layouts. On aarch64 the cost is already present at ff694772 (+6.12 percent, job 224), so it lives in 705, 708 or 730.
JOB=232-arm-hello-705
ISSUE="https://github.com/freeunitorg/benchmarks-drupal"
PHASES="null ab"
WORKLOAD=php-hello
RUNTIME_A=freeunit
RUNTIME_B=freeunit-master-705
SITE=hello
DB=mysql
NO_DB=1
CONNS=32
WARM=2
DUR=10
REPS=4
PERF=0
SERVER_CPUS=0
LOAD_CPUS=1
DB_CPUS=
PRIMARY=server_us
NULL_LIMIT_PCT=5
EXPECT="if this commit is where the aarch64 cost was introduced, the delta is already positive here and stays positive at the tip"
FALSIFY="a level result, which would push the cost to a later commit"
